  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div id=\"\"> <p>APOD</p> <p>Astronomy Picture of the Day</p> <p> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer. </p> <div><p><img width=\"4298\" height=\"3394\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=4298&amp;h=3394&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"Before image of the Andromeda galaxy with streaks marring the field of view.\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=4298&amp;h=3394&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 4298w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=300&amp;h=237&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=768&amp;h=606&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=809&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=1213&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=1617&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=400&amp;h=316&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=600&amp;h=474&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=900&amp;h=711&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=948&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31Before_Scherer_4298.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1579&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 4298px) 100vw, 4298px\"><img width=\"960\" height=\"758\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=960&amp;h=758&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"Image of the Andromeda Galaxy after processing out blemishes.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=960&amp;h=758&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 960w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=300&amp;h=237&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=768&amp;h=606&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=400&amp;h=316&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=600&amp;h=474&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/M31After_Scherer_960.jpg?w=900&amp;h=711&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"></p></div> <div> <p><strong>Explanation:</strong> What does the Andromeda galaxy really look like? The <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/kees-scherer/48847775697/\">featured before image</a> shows how our <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-milky-way-galaxy/\">Milky Way Galaxy</a>'s closest major galactic neighbor really appears in a long exposure through <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/\">Earth</a>'s busy skies and with a digital camera that introduces normal imperfections. The picture is a stack of 223 images, each a 300 second exposure, taken from a garden observatory in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portugal\">Por</a><a href=\"https://youtu.be/ean0YNvdmZI\">t</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portugal\">ugal</a> during 2019. Obvious image deficiencies include bright parallel <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap070825.html\">airplane trails</a>, long and continuous <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap080604.html\">satellite trails</a>, short <a href=\"https://www.eso.org/~ohainaut/ccd/CCD_artifacts.html\">cosmic ray streaks</a>, and <a href=\"https://photographylife.com/dead-vs-stuck-vs-hot-pixels\">bad pixels</a>.  In the after image, these imperfections were actually not removed with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Photoshop\">Photoshop</a> specifically, but rather greatly reduced with a series of computer software packages that included Astro Pixel Processor, DeepSkyStacker, and PixInsight. All of this work was done not to <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/photos/brown-and-white-medium-coated-dog-MjKUUaYQQ6U\">deceive you</a> with a <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap131230.html\">digital fantasy</a> that has little to do with the real likeness of the <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2024-september-8-m31-the-andromeda-galaxy/\">Andromeda galaxy</a> (M31), but to minimize Earthly artifacts that have nothing to do with the distant galaxy and so better recreate <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap190909.html\">what M31 really does look like</a>.</p><p><strong>APOD's email for image submissions has changed.</strong> Please see: <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/lib/apsubmit2015.html\">APOD Submissions</a><br><strong>APOD's main NASA site is <a href=\"https://asterisk.apod.com/viewtopic.php?t=45023\">moving</a>:</strong> From <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/\">apod.nasa.gov</a> to <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod\">science.nasa.gov/apod</a><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture: </strong>cosmic latte </p></div> </div></div>",
